ask(1919,'fairness','Bias & Fairness uneven-performance and validation bullets','In a supplied robot-perception test, group A has 196 correct results out of 200 and group B has 12 out of 20. Which report best exposes a disparity hidden by pooling?', [('Pooled accuracy is about 94.55%, but group B accuracy is 60%','There are208 correct predictions out of220 overall, while12/20=0.60 for B; pooling weights the larger group heavily.'),('Pooled accuracy is 79%, and group B accuracy is 60%','79% is the unweighted mean of98% and60%, not the pooled count-weighted accuracy.'),('Pooled accuracy is about 94.55%, and group B accuracy is also about 94.55%','Applying the pooled metric to each group conceals the observed disparity.')],kind='numerical',difficulty='medium',ass=ACC['assumptions'],formulas=[ACC],steps=['Compute A accuracy:196/200=0.98.','Compute B accuracy:12/20=0.60.','Pool counts:(196+12)/(200+20)=208/220≈0.94545, or94.55%.','Compare group metrics as well as the aggregate; this does not by itself establish every aspect of fairness.'])
